#4471 was merged as one bug. The reports hold **two**, with different causes and different fixes.
The export lists 427 rows, but 15 are repeats of the same id. Counted once each, there are
**412 reports**.

<Callout>
Not one issue. The parser fix covers 379 reports and is fixed. The other 33 will not be fixed: the booking-v3 form is retired.
</Callout>

## The two problems

- **`parser` · 379 reports.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants that write
  the day first get dates flipped. Desk: **fixed** (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). Ticket: [stmizu/firstepisode#1](https://github.com/stmizu/firstepisode/issues/1).
- **`hint` · 33 reports.** The `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People at
  day-first tenants (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) type what the hint says.
  Desk: **won't fix** (booking-v3 form retired). Ticket: [stmizu/firstepisode#2](https://github.com/stmizu/firstepisode/issues/2).

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## How the desk can tell them apart

- Do not trust the intake tag. It is a guess from the browser. It was wrong on 23 `parser`
  reports and on 15 `hint` reports.
- Look up the tenant: its locale and its booking form decide the cause.
- A `form` report from a `booking-v3` tenant that writes the day first is `hint`. Anything else
  from a day-first tenant is `parser`.

## Lessons

- Merging on the subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) hid a second bug.
  A count of 412 looked like one cause.
- Count by id, not by row: exports overlap.
- 5 reports read as a one-day move (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620). They are counted
  under `parser` by tenant. Check them now that the parser fix has shipped.

